      "name": "crew_service_quality",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A genuine categorical axis for grouping crew experiences, useful for the exploratory query. However groundedness is undermined: row 2 mentions nothing about crew yet was labelled 'rude_dismissive', an invented negative that contradicts the silence of the text; a NULL/not-stated would have been correct. Other samples are well-read."
    },
    {
      "name": "seat_hardware_condition",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Useful new axis on physical cabin condition with a sensible NULL for silent rows. But row 2 describes seats as 'dreadful'/'poor padding' yet was labelled 'adequate_functional', contradicting the text; row 1's 'new_excellent' is a stretch from 'well sanitized'. Mixed grounding."
    },
    {
      "name": "food_quality_assessment",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Distinct, groupable food dimension with appropriate NULLs. However row 2 says nothing about food but was labelled 'poor_inedible', an invented value; text-supported rows are read well."
    },
    {
      "name": "special_meal_handling",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.4,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Highly skewed boolean (832/68) with limited analytical leverage for a general 'what's worth analyzing' query. The False values in samples are consistent with texts that don't mention special meals, so grounding is reasonable."
    },
    {
      "name": "disruption_handling_quality",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A meaningful axis distinguishing how disruptions were handled, with a dominant 'no_disruption' default that correctly reflects silent rows. Sample labels align with texts."
    },
    {
      "name": "service_decline_signal",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.45,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A bare boolean flag that largely restates negative crew/service signal already captured by crew_service_quality; limited independent leverage. Sample values (all False) are consistent with the texts."
    },
    {
      "name": "premium_economy_value_gap",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.35,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Very rare True (50/900) boolean of narrow scope; low leverage for a broad exploratory query. It also presumes a premium-economy value judgment often not stated; defaulting to False is defensible but the concept is weakly supported by most texts."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.68,
  "source_groundedness": 0.65,
  "rationale": "The set offers several genuinely useful categorical axes (crew, seat, food, disruption handling) that let the analyst group and compare aspects, directly serving the 'which aspect is worth analyzing' query; a few booleans (special_meal, service_decline, premium_economy_gap) are skewed or redundant and add little. Groundedness is moderate: silent-row NULLs and defaults are handled well, but the aspect-categorization columns show a recurring failure on row 2, where crew, seat, and food were assigned confident (and even contradicting) values despite the text supporting only the seat complaint — indicating over-eager labelling of unmentioned aspects."
}
